#: lib/utility.php
msgid "MariaDB 10.5+ and MySQL 8.0+ are the recommended, supported releases (for example, the default database streams on Rocky Linux 9). Make sure you run the very latest release though which fixes a long standing low level networking issue that was causing spine many issues with reliability."
msgstr "MariaDB 10.5+ na MySQL 8.0+ bụ ụdị a tụrụ aro ma kwado (dịka ọmụmaatụ, iyi nchekwa data ndabara na Rocky Linux 9). Agbanyeghị, jide n'aka na ị na-agba ụdị kachasị ọhụrụ nke na-edozi nsogbu netwọkụ dị ala dịteworo aka nke na-akpatara spine ọtụtụ nsogbu ntụkwasị obi."

#: lib/utility.php
#, php-format
msgid "It is STRONGLY recommended that you enable InnoDB in any %s version greater than 5.5.3."
msgstr "A na-atụ aro ya NKE UKWU ka ị gbanye InnoDB na ụdị %s ọ bụla karịrị 5.5.3."

#: lib/utility.php
msgid "When using Cacti with languages other than English, it is important to use the utf8mb4_unicode_ci collation type as some characters take more than a single byte."
msgstr "Mgbe ị na-eji Cacti na asụsụ ndị ọzọ na-abụghị Bekee, ọ dị mkpa iji ụdị nhazi utf8mb4_unicode_ci n'ihi na ụfọdụ mkpụrụedemede na-ewe karịa otu baịtị."

#: lib/utility.php
msgid "When using Cacti with languages other than English, it is important to use the utf8mb4 character set as some characters take more than a single byte."
msgstr "Mgbe ị na-eji Cacti na asụsụ ndị ọzọ na-abụghị Bekee, ọ dị mkpa iji usoro mkpụrụedemede utf8mb4 n'ihi na ụfọdụ mkpụrụedemede na-ewe karịa otu baịtị."

#: lib/utility.php
#, php-format
msgid "It is recommended that you enable InnoDB in any %s version greater than 5.1."
msgstr "A na-atụ aro ka ị gbanye InnoDB na ụdị %s ọ bụla karịrị 5.1."

#: lib/utility.php
#, php-format
msgid "Depending on the number of logins and use of spine data collector, %s will need many connections.  The calculation for spine is: total_connections = total_processes * (total_threads + script_servers + 1), then you must leave headroom for user connections, which will change depending on the number of concurrent login accounts."
msgstr "Dabere na ọnụọgụgụ nbanye na ojiji nke onye nchịkọta data spine, %s ga-achọ ọtụtụ njikọ. Ngụkọta maka spine bụ: total_connections = total_processes * (total_threads + script_servers + 1), mgbe ahụ ị ga-ahapụrịrị ohere maka njikọ ndị ọrụ, nke ga-agbanwe dabere na ọnụọgụgụ akaụntụ na-abanye n'otu oge."

#: lib/utility.php
msgid "Keeping the table cache larger means less file open/close operations when using innodb_file_per_table."
msgstr "Idobe ebe nchekwa tebụl ka ọ buo ibu pụtara obere ọrụ imeghe/imechi faịlụ mgbe a na-eji innodb_file_per_table."

#: lib/utility.php
msgid "With Remote polling capabilities, large amounts of data will be synced from the main server to the remote pollers.  Therefore, keep this value at or above 16M."
msgstr "Site na ikike nnyocha dịpụrụ adịpụ, a ga-emekọrịta nnukwu data site na sava isi gaa na ndị nnyocha dịpụrụ adịpụ. Ya mere, debe ọnụọgụgụ a na 16M ma ọ bụ karịa."

#: lib/utility.php
#, php-format
msgid "If using the Cacti Performance Booster and choosing a memory storage engine, you have to be careful to flush your Performance Booster buffer before the system runs out of memory table space.  This is done two ways, first reducing the size of your output column to just the right size.  This column is in the tables poller_output, and poller_output_boost.  The second thing you can do is allocate more memory to memory tables.  We have arbitrarily chosen a recommended value of 10%% of system memory, but if you are using SSD disk drives, or have a smaller system, you may ignore this recommendation or choose a different storage engine.  You may see the expected consumption of the Performance Booster tables under Console -> System Utilities -> View Boost Status."
msgstr "Ọ bụrụ na ị na-eji Cacti Performance Booster ma họrọ injin nchekwa nke memory, ị ga-akpachara anya ikpochapụ buffer Performance Booster gị tupu sistemụ agwụsịa ohere tebụl memory. A na-eme nke a n'ụzọ abụọ, nke mbụ bụ ibelata nha kọlụm mmepụta gị ruo nha kwesịrị ekwesị. Kọlụm a dị na tebụl poller_output, na poller_output_boost. Ihe nke abụọ ị nwere ike ime bụ ikenye tebụl memory ohere memory karịrị akarị. Anyị ahọrọla n'atụmatụ uru a tụrụ aro nke 10%% nke memory sistemụ, mana ọ bụrụ na ị na-eji draịvụ diski SSD, ma ọ bụ nwee sistemụ dị ntakịrị, ị nwere ike ileghara ndụmọdụ a anya ma ọ bụ họrọ injin nchekwa dị iche. Ị nwere ike ịhụ ojiji a tụrụ anya ya nke tebụl Performance Booster n'okpuru Console -> System Utilities -> View Boost Status."

#: lib/utility.php
msgid "When executing subqueries, having a larger temporary table size, keep those temporary tables in memory."
msgstr "Mgbe ị na-eme subqueries, inwe nha tebụl nwa oge buru ibu na-edebe tebụl nwa oge ndị ahụ na memory."

#: lib/utility.php
msgid "When performing joins, if they are below this size, they will be kept in memory and never written to a temporary file.  As this is a per connection memory allocation, care must be taken not to increase it too high.  The sum of the join_buffer_size + sort_buffer_size + read_buffer_size + read_rnd_buffer_size + thread_stack + binlog_cache_size + Core MySQL/MariaDB memory should be below 80%.  If the recommendation is negative, you must decrease this and or the sort_buffer_size until the recommendation fits within the allowable memory."
msgstr "Mgbe a na-eme njikọ (joins), ọ bụrụ na ha dị n'okpuru nha a, a ga-edobe ha na ebe nchekwa (memory) ma ọ dịghị mgbe a ga-ede ha na faịlụ nwa oge.  Ebe ọ bụ na nke a bụ oke ebe nchekwa maka njikọ ọ bụla, a ga-akpachara anya ka e wee ghara ibuli ya elu nke ukwuu.  Ngụkọta nke join_buffer_size + sort_buffer_size + read_buffer_size + read_rnd_buffer_size + thread_stack + binlog_cache_size + ebe nchekwa isi MySQL/MariaDB kwesịrị ịdị n'okpuru 80%.  Ọ bụrụ na ndụmọdụ ahụ adịghị mma (negative), ị ga-ebelata nke a na/ma ọ bụ sort_buffer_size ruo mgbe ndụmọdụ ahụ dabara n'ime ebe nchekwa e kwere."

#: lib/utility.php
#, php-format
msgid "When using InnoDB storage it is important to keep your table spaces separate.  This makes managing the tables simpler for long time users of %s.  If you are running with this currently off, you can migrate to the per file storage by enabling the feature, and then running an alter statement on all InnoDB tables."
msgstr "Mgbe ị na-eji nchekwa InnoDB, ọ dị mkpa idowe ohere tebụl gị iche iche. Nke a na-eme ka ijikwa tebụl dịkwuo mfe maka ndị jiworo %s ogologo oge. Ọ bụrụ na ị na-arụ ọrụ ugbu a ka nke a gbanyụrụ, ị nwere ike ịkwaga na nchekwa faịlụ ọ bụla site n'ịgbanye atụmatụ a, wee mee nkwupụta alter na tebụl InnoDB niile."

#: lib/utility.php
msgid "When using innodb_file_per_table, it is important to set the innodb_file_format to Barracuda.  This setting will allow longer indexes important for certain Cacti tables."
msgstr "Mgbe ị na-eji innodb_file_per_table, ọ dị mkpa ịtọ innodb_file_format ka ọ bụrụ Barracuda. Ntọala a ga-enye ohere maka ndeksi ndị toro ogologo karị nke dị mkpa maka ụfọdụ tebụl Cacti."

#: lib/utility.php
msgid "If your tables have very large indexes, you must operate with the Barracuda innodb_file_format and the innodb_large_prefix equal to 1.  Failure to do this may result in plugins that can not properly create tables."
msgstr "Ọ bụrụ na tebụl gị nwere ndeksi buru ibu nke ukwuu, ị ga-arụ ọrụ na innodb_file_format Barracuda yana innodb_large_prefix hà ka 1. Ịghara ime nke a nwere ike ime ka plugins ghara inwe ike ịmepụta tebụl nke ọma."

#: lib/utility.php
#, php-format
msgid "InnoDB will hold as much tables and indexes in system memory as is possible.  Therefore, you should make the innodb_buffer_pool large enough to hold as much of the tables and index in memory.  Checking the size of the /var/lib/mysql/cacti directory will help in determining this value.  We are recommending 25%% of your systems total memory, but your requirements will vary depending on your systems size."
msgstr "InnoDB ga-ejide ọtụtụ tebụl na ndepụta (indexes) na ebe nchekwa sistemụ dị ka o kwere mee.  Ya mere, ị kwesịrị ime ka innodb_buffer_pool buo ibu zuru oke iji jide ọtụtụ tebụl na ndepụta na ebe nchekwa.  Ịlele nha nke ndekọ /var/lib/mysql/cacti ga-enyere aka n'ịchọpụta uru a.  Anyị na-atụ aro 25%% nke ngụkọta ebe nchekwa sistemụ gị, mana mkpa gị ga-adị iche dabere na nha sistemụ gị."

#: lib/utility.php
msgid "This settings should remain ON unless your Cacti instances is running on either ZFS or FusionI/O which both have internal journaling to accommodate abrupt system crashes.  However, if you have very good power, and your systems rarely go down and you have backups, turning this setting to OFF can net you almost a 50% increase in database performance."
msgstr "Ntọala a kwesịrị ịdịgide na ON belụsọ ma ọ bụrụ na Cacti gị na-agba na ZFS ma ọ bụ FusionI/O nke ha abụọ nwere ndekọ dị n'ime (internal journaling) iji nagide ọdịda sistemụ mberede.  Agbanyeghị, ọ bụrụ na ị nwere ọkụ eletrik dị mma nke ukwuu, ma sistemụ gị anaghị adakarị ada, ị nwekwara nchekwa ndabere, ịtụgharị ntọala a gaa na OFF nwere ike inye gị ihe fọrọ nke nta ka ọ bụrụ mmụba 50% na arụmọrụ nchekwa data."

#: lib/utility.php
msgid "This is where metadata is stored. If you had a lot of tables, it would be useful to increase this."
msgstr "Nke a bụ ebe a na-echekwa metadata. Ọ bụrụ na i nwere ọtụtụ tebụl, ọ ga-aba uru ịbawanye nke a."

#: lib/utility.php
msgid "Rogue queries should not for the database to go offline to others.  Kill these queries before they kill your system."
msgstr "Ajụjụ ndị na-akpa aghara ekwesịghị ime ka nchekwa data kwụsị ịrụ ọrụ nye ndị ọzọ. Gbupụ ajụjụ ndị a tupu ha emebie sistemụ gị."

#: lib/utility.php
msgid "Maximum I/O performance happens when you use the O_DIRECT method to flush pages."
msgstr "Arụmọrụ I/O kachasị elu na-eme mgbe i ji usoro O_DIRECT ehichapụ peeji."

#: lib/utility.php
#, php-format
msgid "Setting this value to 2 means that you will flush all transactions every second rather than at commit.  This allows %s to perform writing less often."
msgstr "Ịtọ ọnụ ahịa a ka ọ bụrụ 2 pụtara na ị ga-ekpochapụ azụmahịa niile kwa sekọnd kama ịbụ mgbe e mechara ya. Nke a na-enye %s ohere ide ihe obere oge."

#: lib/utility.php
msgid "With modern SSD type storage, having multiple io threads is advantageous for applications with high io characteristics."
msgstr "Site na nchekwa ụdị SSD nke oge a, inwe ọtụtụ eriri io bara uru maka ngwa nwere njirimara io dị elu."

#: lib/utility.php
#, php-format
msgid "As of %s %s, the you can control how often %s flushes transactions to disk.  The default is 1 second, but in high I/O systems setting to a value greater than 1 can allow disk I/O to be more sequential"
msgstr "Malite na %1$s %2$s, ị nwere ike ijikwa ugboro ole %3$s na-ekpochapụ azụmahịa gaa na diski. Ndabara bụ sekọnd 1, mana na sistemụ I/O dị elu ịtọ ya na ọnụ ahịa karịrị 1 nwere ike ikwe ka I/O diski na-agba n'usoro"

#: lib/utility.php
msgid "With modern SSD type storage, having multiple read io threads is advantageous for applications with high io characteristics.  Depending on your MariaDB/MySQL versions, this value can go as high as 64.  But try to keep the number less than your total SMT threads on the database server."
msgstr "Site na nchekwa ụdị SSD nke oge a, inwe ọtụtụ eriri ọgụgụ io bara uru maka ngwa nwere njirimara io dị elu. Dabere na nsụgharị MariaDB/MySQL gị, ọnụ ahịa a nwere ike iru 64. Mana gbalịa idobe ọnụọgụ ahụ ka ọ dị obere karịa mkpokọta eriri SMT gị na sava nchekwa data."

#: lib/utility.php
msgid "With modern SSD type storage, having multiple write io threads is advantageous for applications with high io characteristics.  Depending on your MariaDB/MySQL versions, this value can go as high as 64.  But try to keep the number less than your total SMT threads on the database server."
msgstr "Site na nchekwa ụdị SSD nke oge a, inwe ọtụtụ eriri edemede io bara uru maka ngwa nwere njirimara io dị elu. Dabere na nsụgharị MariaDB/MySQL gị, ọnụ ahịa a nwere ike iru 64. Mana gbalịa idobe ọnụọgụ ahụ ka ọ dị obere karịa mkpokọta eriri SMT gị na sava nchekwa data."

#: lib/utility.php
#, php-format
msgid "%s will divide the innodb_buffer_pool into memory regions to improve performance for versions of MariaDB less than 10.5.  The max value is 64, but should not exceed more than the number of CPU cores/threads.  When your innodb_buffer_pool is less than 1GB, you should use the pool size divided by 128MB.  Continue to use this equation up to the max the number of CPU cores or 64."
msgstr "%s ga-ekewa innodb_buffer_pool ka ọ bụrụ mpaghara ebe nchekwa iji melite arụmọrụ maka nsụgharị MariaDB ndị dị n'okpuru 10.5. Ọnụ ahịa kachasị elu bụ 64, mana o kwesịghị ịkarị ọnụọgụgụ CPU cores/eriri. Mgbe innodb_buffer_pool gị dị obere karịa 1GB, i kwesịrị iji nha ọdọ mmiri ahụ kewaa site na 128MB. Gaa n'ihu na-eji nhata a ruo na nke kachasị elu n'ọnụọgụgụ CPU cores ma ọ bụ 64."

#: lib/utility.php
#, php-format
msgid "%s will divide the innodb_buffer_pool into memory regions to improve performance for versions of MySQL upto and including MySQL 8.0.  The max value is 64, but should not exceed more than the number of CPU cores/threads.  When your innodb_buffer_pool is less than 1GB, you should use the pool size divided by 128MB.  Continue to use this equation up to the max of the number of CPU cores or 64."
msgstr "%s ga-ekewa innodb_buffer_pool ka ọ bụrụ mpaghara ebe nchekwa iji melite arụmọrụ maka nsụgharị MySQL ruo ma gụnye MySQL 8.0. Ọnụ ahịa kachasị elu bụ 64, mana o kwesịghị ịkarị ọnụọgụgụ CPU cores/eriri. Mgbe innodb_buffer_pool gị dị obere karịa 1GB, i kwesịrị iji nha ọdọ mmiri ahụ kewaa site na 128MB. Gaa n'ihu na-eji nhata a ruo na nke kachasị elu n'ọnụọgụgụ CPU cores ma ọ bụ 64."

#: lib/utility.php
msgid "If you have SSD disks, use this suggestion.  If you have physical hard drives, use 200 * the number of active drives in the array.  If using NVMe or PCIe Flash, much larger numbers as high as 100000 can be used."
msgstr "Ọ bụrụ na i nwere diski SSD, jiri aro a. Ọ bụrụ na i nwere draịvụ ike nkịtị, jiri 200 * ọnụọgụ draịvụ na-arụ ọrụ n'usoro ahụ. Ọ bụrụ na ị na-eji NVMe ma ọ bụ PCIe Flash, a pụrụ iji ọnụọgụ buru ibu nke ukwuu ruru 100000."

#: lib/utility.php
msgid "If you have SSD disks, use this suggestion.  If you have physical hard drives, use 2000 * the number of active drives in the array.  If using NVMe or PCIe Flash, much larger numbers as high as 200000 can be used."
msgstr "Ọ bụrụ na i nwere diski SSD, jiri aro a. Ọ bụrụ na i nwere draịvụ ike nkịtị, jiri 2000 * ọnụọgụ draịvụ na-arụ ọrụ n'usoro ahụ. Ọ bụrụ na ị na-eji NVMe ma ọ bụ PCIe Flash, a pụrụ iji ọnụọgụ buru ibu nke ukwuu ruru 200000."

#: lib/utility.php
msgid "If you have SSD disks, set this to 0. Otherwise, do not set this setting."
msgstr "Ọ bụrụ na i nwere diski SSD, tọọ nke a ka ọ bụrụ 0. Ma ọ bụghị ya, atọla ntọala a."

#: lib/utility.php
msgid "With modern SSD type storage, having multiple read io threads is advantageous for applications with high io characteristics."
msgstr "Site na nchekwa ụdị SSD nke oge a, inwe ọtụtụ eriri ọgụgụ io bara uru maka ngwa nwere njirimara io dị elu."

#: lib/utility.php
msgid "With modern SSD type storage, having multiple write io threads is advantageous for applications with high io characteristics."
msgstr "Site na nchekwa ụdị SSD nke oge a, inwe ọtụtụ eriri edemede io bara uru maka ngwa nwere njirimara io dị elu."

#: lib/utility.php
msgid "When using MariaDB 10.2.4 and above, this setting should be off if atomic writes are enabled.  Therefore, please enable atomic writes instead of the double write buffer as it will increase performance."
msgstr "Mgbe ị na-eji MariaDB 10.2.4 na nke karịrị ya, ntọala a kwesịrị ịgbanyụ ma ọ bụrụ na agbanyere edemede atomic. Ya mere, biko gbanye edemede atomic kama iji ihe nchekwa edemede abụọ n'ihi na ọ ga-abawanye arụmọrụ."

#: lib/utility.php
msgid "When using MariaDB 10.2.4 and above, you can use atomic writes over the doublewrite buffer to increase performance."
msgstr "Mgbe ị na-eji MariaDB 10.2.4 na nke karịrị ya, ị nwere ike iji edemede atomic karịa ihe nchekwa doublewrite iji bawanye arụmọrụ."

